    "body": "I think the date is reasonably part of the caption, similarly for credit. In particular the date is not in itself the figure -- the image is. It seems a bit confusing to reason about what was intended if flow content is allowed both before and after `figcaption`.\r\n\r\n```html\r\n<figure>\r\n  <img src=\"duck.jpg\">\r\n  <figcaption>\r\n    <div>The yellow duck splashes in the water</div>\r\n    <div>Picture taken: <time>2011-11-18</time></div>\r\n  </figcaption>\r\n</figure>\r\n```\r\n\r\nOrder often does matter in HTML (e.g. `table`, `fieldset`...).",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
